# ============================================================
# Shared .gitignore base — universal concerns
# ============================================================
# This is the single source of truth for ignore patterns that apply
# to ALL projects generated from these boilerplates, regardless of
# language or framework. Template .gitignore files include this via:
#
#   {-% include "partials.bak/partials/gitignore-partials/gitignore-base.jinja" %-}  (remove dashes)
#
# and append only their language/framework-specific patterns below.
#
# Patterns are curated from the ignorefile-manager skill's concern
# sources (os-files, editor-files, secrets, logs, vcs-meta, dev-local,
# and universal build-artifacts). Language-specific build artifacts,
# dependencies, and lockfiles belong in the per-template .gitignore.

